-- TESTS — Part 4 (ss 42-75), regs 26-30 and Schedule 2.

§ `Tests — administration and enforcement`

GIVEN a   IS AN Authorisation
      emp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Officer
`an officer` a `, employee:` emp MEANS Officer WITH `authorisation` IS a, `an employee of the local government` IS emp

`the ranger`   MEANS `an officer` `appointed under the Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2) for the purposes of the Cat Act` `, employee:` TRUE
`a constable`  MEANS `an officer` `a police officer` `, employee:` FALSE
`a clerk`      MEANS `an officer` `no authorisation under the Cat Act` `, employee:` TRUE

§§ `s 43(2)`

#ASSERT     `regarded as within the district under s 43(2):` FALSE `,` TRUE  `,` FALSE
#ASSERT     `regarded as within the district under s 43(2):` FALSE `,` FALSE `,` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `regarded as within the district under s 43(2):` FALSE `,` FALSE `,` FALSE

§§ `ss 44-47 — delegations`

GIVEN dfrom   IS A Delegator
      dto     IS A Delegate
      isAP    IS A BOOLEAN
      written IS A BOOLEAN
      absMaj  IS A BOOLEAN
      section IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Delegation
`a delegation by` dfrom `to` dto `, an authorised person:` isAP `, written:` written `, absolute majority:` absMaj `, of a power under s` section MEANS
    Delegation WITH
        `delegator`                        IS dfrom
        `delegate`                         IS dto
        `delegate is an authorised person` IS isAP
        `in writing`                       IS written
        `decided by an absolute majority`  IS absMaj
        `power or duty under section`      IS section

#ASSERT     `a valid delegation under s 44` (`a delegation by` `the local government` `to` `the CEO of the local government` `, an authorised person:` FALSE `, written:` TRUE  `, absolute majority:` TRUE  `, of a power under s` 9)
#ASSERT NOT `a valid delegation under s 44` (`a delegation by` `the local government` `to` `the CEO of the local government` `, an authorised person:` FALSE `, written:` TRUE  `, absolute majority:` FALSE `, of a power under s` 9)
#ASSERT NOT `a valid delegation under s 44` (`a delegation by` `the local government` `to` `the CEO of the local government` `, an authorised person:` FALSE `, written:` FALSE `, absolute majority:` TRUE  `, of a power under s` 9)
#ASSERT NOT `a valid delegation under s 44` (`a delegation by` `the local government` `to` `an employee of the local government` `, an authorised person:` FALSE `, written:` TRUE  `, absolute majority:` TRUE  `, of a power under s` 9)
#ASSERT     `a valid delegation under s 45` (`a delegation by` `the CEO` `to` `an employee of the local government` `, an authorised person:` TRUE  `, written:` TRUE  `, absolute majority:` FALSE `, of a power under s` 26)
-- (6): a power under s 63, 64 or 65 cannot go to an authorised person ...
#ASSERT NOT `a valid delegation under s 45` (`a delegation by` `the CEO` `to` `an employee of the local government` `, an authorised person:` TRUE  `, written:` TRUE  `, absolute majority:` FALSE `, of a power under s` 64)
-- ... but may go to an employee who is not one.
#ASSERT     `a valid delegation under s 45` (`a delegation by` `the CEO` `to` `an employee of the local government` `, an authorised person:` FALSE `, written:` TRUE  `, absolute majority:` FALSE `, of a power under s` 64)
#ASSERT NOT `a valid delegation under s 45` (`a delegation by` `the CEO` `to` `another person` `, an authorised person:` FALSE `, written:` TRUE  `, absolute majority:` FALSE `, of a power under s` 26)

-- s 46(1)(a): no period specified — indefinitely.
#ASSERT     `a delegation made on` (YMD 2025 10 1) `and ending on` NOTHING `has effect on` (YMD 2035 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `a delegation made on` (YMD 2025 10 1) `and ending on` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30)) `has effect on` (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT     `a delegation made on` (YMD 2025 10 1) `and ending on` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30)) `has effect on` (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- s 47(2): the financial year ending 30 June 2026 runs from 1 July 2025.
#ASSERT     `the delegations were reviewed in the financial year ending 30 June` 2026 `, reviewed on` (LIST YMD 2025 7 1)
#ASSERT     `the delegations were reviewed in the financial year ending 30 June` 2026 `, reviewed on` (LIST YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the delegations were reviewed in the financial year ending 30 June` 2026 `, reviewed on` (LIST YMD 2025 6 30, YMD 2026 7 1)

