§§ `Schedule 2 — every row`

#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 5(1) — cat not registered`                                     EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 1 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 6(1) — registered cat in a public place not wearing its tag`   EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 2 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 7 — removing or interfering with a registration tag`           EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 3 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 14(1) — cat not microchipped`                                  EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 4 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 17 — removing or interfering with a microchip`                 EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 5 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 18(1) — cat not sterilised`                                    EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 6 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 19 — identifying as sterilised a cat that is not`              EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 7 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 23(1) — transferring a cat that is not microchipped`           EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 8 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 23(2) — transferring a cat that is not sterilised`             EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 9 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 24 — seller not giving notice of a transfer`                   EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 10 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 25 — owner not giving notice of a change to recorded information` EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 11 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 35(1) — breeding cats without approval`                        EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 12 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 41 — offering a cat as a prize`                                EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 13 200
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 50(2) — refusing to give name, residence and date of birth`    EQUALS `prescribed in Schedule 2` 14 200
-- Offences Schedule 2 does not list.
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 15 — implanter not giving the database company the prescribed information` EQUALS `not prescribed by the Cat Regulations 2012; a local law may prescribe it`
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 30(1) — facility operator not attempting to identify the owner` EQUALS `not prescribed by the Cat Regulations 2012; a local law may prescribe it`
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `s 85 — false or misleading information`                          EQUALS `not prescribed by the Cat Regulations 2012; a local law may prescribe it`
#ASSERT `the Schedule 2 entry for` `reg 5(3) — implanting a non-complying microchip`                 EQUALS `not prescribed by the Cat Regulations 2012; a local law may prescribe it`

-- s 63(3): $200 is within 10% of $5 000 ($500), for every offence.
`every offence` MEANS LIST
    `s 5(1) — cat not registered`, `s 6(1) — registered cat in a public place not wearing its tag`, `s 7 — removing or interfering with a registration tag`
    , `s 14(1) — cat not microchipped`, `s 15 — implanter not giving the database company the prescribed information`, `s 16 — database company not keeping the prescribed information`
    , `s 17 — removing or interfering with a microchip`, `s 18(1) — cat not sterilised`, `s 19 — identifying as sterilised a cat that is not`
    , `s 20 — veterinarian not notifying the database company of a sterilisation`, `s 21 — veterinarian not giving a certificate of sterilisation`
    , `s 23(1) — transferring a cat that is not microchipped`, `s 23(2) — transferring a cat that is not sterilised`, `s 24 — seller not giving notice of a transfer`
    , `s 25 — owner not giving notice of a change to recorded information`, `s 30(1) — facility operator not attempting to identify the owner`
    , `s 32 — facility operator not notifying the owner`, `s 35(1) — breeding cats without approval`, `s 41 — offering a cat as a prize`
    , `s 50(2) — refusing to give name, residence and date of birth`, `s 54 — obstructing an authorised person`, `s 85 — false or misleading information`
    , `reg 5(2) — selling or supplying a non-complying microchip`, `reg 5(3) — implanting a non-complying microchip`
#ASSERT count `every offence` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT all (GIVEN o YIELD `s 63(3) is met by the modified penalty for` o) `every offence`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN o YIELD `the maximum fine for` o EQUALS 5000) `every offence`
-- 14 of the 24 are in Schedule 2.
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN o YIELD NOT (`the Schedule 2 entry for` o EQUALS `not prescribed by the Cat Regulations 2012; a local law may prescribe it`)) `every offence`) EQUALS 14

§§ `s 62 — giving an infringement notice`

GIVEN offence  IS A DATE
      g        IS A DATE
      penalty  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Infringement notice`
`a notice for an offence on` offence `given` g `for` penalty MEANS
    `Infringement notice` WITH
        `date of the alleged offence`   IS offence
        `date given`                    IS g
        `modified penalty specified`    IS penalty
        `extended time to pay, in days` IS 0
        `date paid`                     IS NOTHING
        `date withdrawn`                IS NOTHING

-- 28 days after Mon 1 Dec 2025: Mon 29 Dec.
#ASSERT     `s 62 permits` `the ranger` `to give notice` (`a notice for an offence on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `given` (YMD 2025 12 29) `for` 200) `for` `s 5(1) — cat not registered` `, a local law prescribing` NOTHING `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
#ASSERT NOT `s 62 permits` `the ranger` `to give notice` (`a notice for an offence on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `given` (YMD 2025 12 30) `for` 200) `for` `s 5(1) — cat not registered` `, a local law prescribing` NOTHING `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
-- 28 days after Thu 27 Nov 2025 end on Christmas Day; s 61(1)(e) carries it to Mon 29 Dec.
#ASSERT     `s 62 permits` `the ranger` `to give notice` (`a notice for an offence on` (YMD 2025 11 27) `given` (YMD 2025 12 29) `for` 200) `for` `s 5(1) — cat not registered` `, a local law prescribing` NOTHING `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
-- s 63(2): the notice must specify the prescribed modified penalty.
#ASSERT NOT `s 62 permits` `the ranger` `to give notice` (`a notice for an offence on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `given` (YMD 2025 12 5) `for` 150) `for` `s 5(1) — cat not registered` `, a local law prescribing` NOTHING `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
-- s 62(3): only a local-government employee.
#ASSERT NOT `s 62 permits` `a constable` `to give notice` (`a notice for an offence on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `given` (YMD 2025 12 5) `for` 200) `for` `s 5(1) — cat not registered` `, a local law prescribing` NOTHING `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
-- An offence not in Schedule 2: only if a local law prescribes it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 62 permits` `the ranger` `to give notice` (`a notice for an offence on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `given` (YMD 2025 12 5) `for` 200) `for` `s 85 — false or misleading information` `, a local law prescribing` NOTHING `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
#ASSERT     `s 62 permits` `the ranger` `to give notice` (`a notice for an offence on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `given` (YMD 2025 12 5) `for` 250) `for` `s 85 — false or misleading information` `, a local law prescribing` (JUST 250) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
#ASSERT     `a local government may prescribe the offence under s 62(2):` TRUE `,` TRUE `,` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a local government may prescribe the offence under s 62(2):` TRUE `,` FALSE `,` TRUE

§§ `ss 63-66 — paying, extending, withdrawing`

GIVEN extension IS A NUMBER
      paid      IS A MAYBE DATE
      withdrawn IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `Infringement notice`
`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` extension `, paid` paid `, withdrawn` withdrawn MEANS
    `Infringement notice` WITH
        `date of the alleged offence`   IS YMD 2025 11 28
        `date given`                    IS YMD 2025 12 1
        `modified penalty specified`    IS 200
        `extended time to pay, in days` IS extension
        `date paid`                     IS paid
        `date withdrawn`                IS withdrawn

-- s 63(1)(b): 28 days after Mon 1 Dec — Mon 29 Dec; with a 14-day
-- extension under s 64, 42 days — Mon 12 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day to pay the modified penalty under` (`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` 0  `, paid` NOTHING `, withdrawn` NOTHING) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 29
#ASSERT `the last day to pay the modified penalty under` (`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` 14 `, paid` NOTHING `, withdrawn` NOTHING) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 12
-- s 65(1): "Within one year after the notice was given": through 1 Dec 2026.
#ASSERT     `on` (YMD 2026 12 1) `the CEO may withdraw` (`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` 0 `, paid` NOTHING `, withdrawn` NOTHING) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
#ASSERT NOT `on` (YMD 2026 12 2) `the CEO may withdraw` (`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` 0 `, paid` NOTHING `, withdrawn` NOTHING) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
-- s 65(1) with Interpretation Act s 61(1)(e): a notice given Fri 2 Oct 2026;
-- the year ends Sat 2 Oct 2027, so withdrawal is still in time on Mon 4 Oct
-- and not on Tue 5 Oct. (This case was found by the independent test pass.)
#ASSERT     `on` (YMD 2027 10 4) `the CEO may withdraw` (`Infringement notice` WITH `date of the alleged offence` IS YMD 2026 10 1, `date given` IS YMD 2026 10 2, `modified penalty specified` IS 200, `extended time to pay, in days` IS 0, `date paid` IS NOTHING, `date withdrawn` IS NOTHING) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
#ASSERT NOT `on` (YMD 2027 10 5) `the CEO may withdraw` (`Infringement notice` WITH `date of the alleged offence` IS YMD 2026 10 1, `date given` IS YMD 2026 10 2, `modified penalty specified` IS 200, `extended time to pay, in days` IS 0, `date paid` IS NOTHING, `date withdrawn` IS NOTHING) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
-- s 65(2): withdrawn after payment — refund.
#ASSERT     `s 65(2) requires a refund under` (`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` 0 `, paid` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 10)) `, withdrawn` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)))
#ASSERT NOT `s 65(2) requires a refund under` (`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` 0 `, paid` NOTHING `, withdrawn` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)))
-- s 66: paid in time and not withdrawn bars proceedings.
#ASSERT     `paying under` (`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` 0  `, paid` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 29)) `, withdrawn` NOTHING) `bars proceedings for the offence, given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
#ASSERT NOT `paying under` (`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` 0  `, paid` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 30)) `, withdrawn` NOTHING) `bars proceedings for the offence, given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
#ASSERT     `paying under` (`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` 14 `, paid` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 10)) `, withdrawn` NOTHING) `bars proceedings for the offence, given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
#ASSERT NOT `paying under` (`a notice given 1 December 2025, extended` 0  `, paid` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 10)) `, withdrawn` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5))) `bars proceedings for the offence, given` `WA holidays 2025-26`

§§ `ss 68-72 — objection and review`

GIVEN dec      IS A `Reviewable decision`
      notified IS A MAYBE DATE
      lodged   IS A MAYBE DATE
      further  IS A NUMBER
      disposed IS A MAYBE DATE
      review   IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `Objection history`
`a history of` dec `; notified` notified `; lodged` lodged `; further time` further `; disposed` disposed `; review` review MEANS
    `Objection history` WITH
        `decision`                                   IS dec
        `date of the decision`                       IS YMD 2025 12 1
        `date notice of the decision was given`      IS notified
        `date objection lodged`                      IS lodged
        `further time allowed by the local government, in days` IS further
        `date notice of disposal of the objection given` IS disposed
        `date review applied for`                    IS review

-- s 69(2): 28 days after notice on Mon 1 Dec — Mon 29 Dec.
#ASSERT     `the objection in` (`a history of` `refusal to grant registration` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 29)) `; further time` 0 `; disposed` NOTHING `; review` NOTHING) `was lodged in time, given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
#ASSERT NOT `the objection in` (`a history of` `refusal to grant registration` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 30)) `; further time` 0 `; disposed` NOTHING `; review` NOTHING) `was lodged in time, given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
-- "or within such further time as the local government may allow": 7 more
-- days runs to 35 days after 1 Dec, Mon 5 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT     `the objection in` (`a history of` `refusal to grant registration` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)) `; further time` 7 `; disposed` NOTHING `; review` NOTHING) `was lodged in time, given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
-- s 69(1): not after applying for review.
#ASSERT NOT `the objection in` (`a history of` `refusal to grant registration` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 20)) `; further time` 0 `; disposed` NOTHING `; review` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 10))) `was lodged in time, given` `WA holidays 2025-26`
-- s 68: only the four decisions.
#ASSERT NOT `the objection in` (`a history of` `another decision` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 5)) `; further time` 0 `; disposed` NOTHING `; review` NOTHING) `was lodged in time, given` `WA holidays 2025-26`

-- s 70(1)-(2)
#ASSERT     `s 70 lets` `the council` `deal with an objection to a decision` `made by the council`
#ASSERT NOT `s 70 lets` `a committee authorised by the council` `deal with an objection to a decision` `made by the council`
#ASSERT NOT `s 70 lets` `a committee authorised by the council` `deal with an objection to a decision` `made by that committee`
#ASSERT     `s 70 lets` `a committee authorised by the council` `deal with an objection to a decision` `made by someone else`

-- s 71. (1)(a): no objection; notice Mon 1 Dec 2025; 42 days — Mon 12 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `the s 71 review window for` (`a history of` `cancellation of registration` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` NOTHING `; further time` 0 `; disposed` NOTHING `; review` NOTHING) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26` EQUALS JUST (`Review window` WITH `route` IS "s 71(1)(a): no objection lodged", `first day` IS YMD 2025 12 1, `last day` IS YMD 2026 1 12)
-- (1)(b): lodged Wed 10 Dec 2025, not disposed of. The section's example (b):
-- "more than 35 days, but within 77 days, after the objection was lodged" —
-- Thu 15 Jan to Wed 25 Feb 2026.
#ASSERT `the s 71 review window for` (`a history of` `cancellation of registration` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 10)) `; further time` 0 `; disposed` NOTHING `; review` NOTHING) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26` EQUALS JUST (`Review window` WITH `route` IS "s 71(1)(b): objection not disposed of within 35 days", `first day` IS YMD 2026 1 15, `last day` IS YMD 2026 2 25)
-- (2): disposed of on Mon 5 Jan 2026; example (c): within 42 days — Mon 16 Feb 2026.
#ASSERT `the s 71 review window for` (`a history of` `cancellation of registration` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 10)) `; further time` 0 `; disposed` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)) `; review` NOTHING) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26` EQUALS JUST (`Review window` WITH `route` IS "s 71(2): review of the decision on the objection", `first day` IS YMD 2026 1 5, `last day` IS YMD 2026 2 16)
#ASSERT `the s 71 review window for` (`a history of` `another decision` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` NOTHING `; further time` 0 `; disposed` NOTHING `; review` NOTHING) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 72: a refusal to RENEW, with an objection pending — suspended.
#ASSERT     `the decision in` (`a history of` `refusal to renew registration` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 10)) `; further time` 0 `; disposed` NOTHING `; review` NOTHING) `is suspended, pending:` TRUE `, Tribunal order against:` FALSE
#ASSERT     `the decision in` (`a history of` `cancellation of an approval to breed` `; notified` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) `; lodged` NOTHING `; further time` 0 `; disposed` NOTHING `; review` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 20))) `is suspended, pending:` TRUE `, Tribunal order against:` FALSE
-- A refusal to GRANT is not listed.
